// MC-PATCH: maic-incomplete-turn-recovery-v2
	// REPLACE: const OLLAMA_INCOMPLETE_TURN_PROVIDER_ID_PATTERN = /^ollama(?:-|$)/;
// Lesson 1127 (2026-10-07, David): MC's main provider is `maic` (MAIC),
// not `ollama`. The default pattern only matches `ollama` / `ollama-*`,
// so the embedded-agent retry guards (resolveReasoningOnlyRetryInstruction,
// resolveEmptyResponseRetryInstruction, isIncompleteTurnRecoverySupportedProviderModel)
// never trigger for `maic/*` providers — every `stopReason=length` falls
// through to the "⚠️ Agent couldn't generate a response" error path. Extending
// the pattern to also accept `maic`/`maic-*` enables automatic reasoning-only
// retries (up to 2) and empty-response retries (up to 1) for MAIC models.
//
// Why this is safe: the retry path only fires on incomplete turns
// (stopReason=length, no visible text, no committed side effects). MAIC
// is a strict-agentic runtime, so the retry instructions are well-defined
// for it. The fix is one regex, additive only — no behavior change for
// existing `ollama` providers.
const OLLAMA_INCOMPLETE_TURN_PROVIDER_ID_PATTERN = /^(?:ollama|maic)(?:-|$)/;
	// REPLACE: 	if (assistant?.stopReason === "stop" && OLLAMA_INCOMPLETE_TURN_PROVIDER_ID_PATTERN.test(normalizeLowercaseStringOrEmpty(params.provider ?? "")) && !hasPositiveOutputTokenUsage(assistant)) return null;
// Lesson 1138 v2-corrected (2026-10-09 23:20 MDT, David): The original
// `!hasPositiveOutputTokenUsage(assistant)` check was correct for ollama
// (don't retry when ollama reports 0 output tokens — the model is in
// reasoning-only mode). But it ALSO fired for MAIC because the embedded
// agent's transform produces `usage.output = 0` for empty responses — so
// adding `maic` to the OLLAMA pattern (Lesson 1127) caused this safety
// guard to incorrectly suppress MAIC's empty-response retry.
//
// Verified 2026-10-09 23:20 MDT via Node isolation test of the patched
// function with the exact params from the sidecar log:
//   provider=maic, modelId=chat-nemotron-super, stopReason=stop,
//   usage={output:0,...}, replayMetadata={hadPotentialSideEffects:false}
//   → GATE3 returned null (suppressed retry) → FINAL RETURN NULL → no retry
//   → empty response surfaced as "Agent couldn't generate a response"
//
// Fix: revert GATE3 to use the ollama-only pattern. The reasoning-model
// safety guard stays ollama-only (its original design). MAIC's empty
// responses should be retried (not suppressed) — that's what the user wants
// for "Hello" prompts where MAIC just returns content=[].
	if (assistant?.stopReason === "stop" && /^ollama(?:-|$)/.test(normalizeLowercaseStringOrEmpty(params.provider ?? "")) && !hasPositiveOutputTokenUsage(assistant)) return null;

// MC-PATCH: maic-empty-retry-debug-v3
